Home Assistant Input Text Entity ID Tracking
Store the source entity ID with the helper text, hide it on the dashboard, and use it for visibility checks.
1. Write the entity ID + dash + your text
- action: input_text.set_value
  target:
    entity_id: input_text.script_tracking
  data:
    value: "{{ this.entity_id }} - Your text here"
Example stored value: automation.workday_wakeup - Security Alert!
2. Display only the text after the entity ID and dash
{{ states('input_text.script_tracking').split(' - ', 1)[1] }}
Displays: Security Alert!
3. Check whether a specific entity ID is stored
{{ states('input_text.script_tracking').startswith('automation.workday_wakeup - ') }}
Result: true when the helper was written with that entity ID; false otherwise.
Dashboard use: Use the third template as a template visibility condition. Change only the entity ID you want to match.
